# Documents that have actually been READ OUT for a person, with the citation.
#
# Why this file exists: tools/coverage.py grades the direct line, and its
# "scanned" state means "an image is attached but has not been read out". It had
# no way of knowing when a document HAD been read, because a reading lives in a
# page's prose or a note, not in the data. So four people sat at "scanned" whose
# documents had been read out weeks earlier, and /coverage overstated how much
# of the line was unevidenced. That was question 9b.
#
# One row per person per document. The slug is the person the document is
# evidence FOR - a baptism names parents, so it is a reading for the child and
# for both parents.
#
# slug|kind|year|where read|citation
